+### §check-fails-closed — any failing command aborts the check with a non-zero exit
+- Since: 2026-10-23 (the user overrode §check-fails-open, below)
+- Decision: `set -euo pipefail`. Any failing command aborts the check with a non-zero exit, which blocks the commit.
+  Large staged files still only produce a warning; a clean run ends in `exit 0`.
+- Forbidden: dropping `-e`; `test && action` as the last command of a loop body (a false test makes the loop, and so
+  the check, exit non-zero on an ordinary commit). Use `if test; then action; fi`.
+- Reason: the maintainer wants the check's own failures to stop the commit instead of being swallowed. The
+  staged-then-deleted file behind the 2026-09-10 incident is skipped by the `[ -f "$f" ] || continue` guard, so it
+  does not abort the check.
+- Rejected: §check-fails-open (2026-09-11, overridden by the user 2026-10-23): `set -uo pipefail` without `-e`, every
+  internal error ending in `exit 0`. Adopted after a `wc` failure on a staged-then-deleted file under `set -e` blocked
+  every commit in the repository for a day (2026-09-10).
